law.text:
		A license issued pursuant to this article may be denied, suspended, or revoked on any one or more of the following grounds, where applicable:

Material misstatement or omission in application for license;


Failure to comply subsequent to receipt of a written notice from the Department or any willful failure to comply with a lawful order, any provision of this article, or any term, condition, or restriction of a license;


Failure to comply with zoning or other land use regulations, ordinances, or statutes;


Use of deceptive business acts or practices;


Knowingly advertising by any means any assertion, representation, or statement of fact that is untrue, misleading, or deceptive relating to the conduct of the business for which a license is held or sought;


Having been found, through a judicial or administrative hearing, to have committed fraudulent or deceptive acts in connection with the training center for which a license is held or sought, or any consumer-related fraud;


Having been convicted of any criminal act involving the training center for which a license is held or sought;


Improper assignment, lending, or otherwise allowing the improper use of a license;


Any corporate officer, owner, administrator and any individual authorized to obligate the training center having been convicted of a felony;


Any corporate officer, owner, administrator and any individual authorized to obligate the training center having been convicted of any misdemeanor involving lying, cheating, stealing, or moral turpitude;


Failure to furnish the Department information, documentation, or records required or requested pursuant to this article;


Knowingly and willfully filing any false report, account, record, or memorandum;


Willfully altering or changing the appearance or wording of a training center license or a course completion certificate;


Failure to provide services in accordance with the terms, limitations, conditions, or requirements of the license; or


Failure to comply with other state and federal requirements relating to training center operations.
